	(text "RAILS (record section 10: independent bucks from +BUS). TPS54560B x3, one layout three times; values from the datasheet's own design procedure (SLVSF00 section 8.2).\nDesign inputs: VIN 20-48 V (48 = supply OVP ceiling, covers the ~45 V clamp; part rated 60 V), 4 A per rail, 400 kHz, half-load step held within 4 %.\n  fsw 400 kHz: RT 243k. Worst on-time 3.3 V at 48 V = 205 ns vs 135 ns minimum.       UVLO: 887k / 53.6k = start 20 V, stop 17 V.\n  12 V: L 18u, Cout 4x 22u/25V (~40u derated), FB 140k/10k = 12.00 V, comp 21.5k + 5.6n (fco ~35 kHz)\n   5 V: L 10u, Cout 3x 47u/10V (~85u derated), FB 52.3k/10k = 4.98 V, comp 15.8k + 6.8n (fco ~28 kHz)\n  3.3V: L 6.8u, Cout 3x 47u/10V (~113u derated), FB 31.6k/10k = 3.33 V, comp 13.7k + 6.8n (fco ~28 kHz)\n  Inductors: Isat >= 7.5 A (the switch current limit, datasheet's conservative rule), shielded. Catch diode B560C (60 V 5 A, datasheet's pick). C106/C206/C306 = optional HF pole, DNP.\nLOADS (operator ruling 2026-09-22): LOGIC runs from the stamp's own rails so a USB-only bench session powers the pulse path:\n  +5V_SYS = stamp pad 39 (its OR of VIN and USB): 74AHCT125, drive 485_5V, status LED.   +3V3_SYS = stamp pad 28: INA228, THVD1450, every pull-up.\n  +5V feeds the stamp's VIN (pad 14) and 5 V accessories. +12V: regen clamp supply, fan, 12 V accessory. +3V3_ACC: 3.3 V accessory only.\nLAYOUT: amp-class switch nodes vs the INA228 resolving +-5 uV is the likeliest respin (section 10). Small SW nodes, far from R2 and U11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 236.22 0)
